"""bug-nilpy-void-def-assigned-and-called-crashes: an explicit `-> None` def
assigned to a plain name and then called through it, generic-dispatch style
(no Callable-typed field/param signature to fall back on), used to segfault
right after the callee's body finished — pybound_callv1 unconditionally cast
the code pointer through a Variant-returning function type, which a real
Pascal procedure (what a `-> None` def compiles to) never sets up.
"""


def hit(vm) -> None:
    print("native ran")


f = hit
f(1)
print("done")
